# Network Attack Analysis – SYN Flood Incident

## Overview
This project analyzes a simulated network security incident involving a web server experiencing service disruption due to abnormal TCP SYN traffic. Using packet capture data (tcpdump/Wireshark-style logs), the objective is to identify the type of network attack, explain how it works at the protocol level, and assess its impact on system availability.

The scenario demonstrates how a Denial of Service (DoS) SYN flood attack can exhaust server resources by exploiting the TCP three-way handshake process.

---

## Skills Demonstrated
- Network traffic analysis (TCP/IP)
- Identifying SYN flood DoS attacks
- Understanding TCP three-way handshake behavior
- Incident analysis and root cause reasoning
- Cybersecurity reporting and documentation

